    <string name="accessibility_service_description">
    Scroll Break requires Accessibility permission to provide its core features.
    With this access, the app can detect which application is on screen, count scroll events, and block distracting apps during Focus Mode. When Smart Scroll Intervention is enabled, it also uses basic view structure to wait for a stopping point. App labels, session duration, intervention outcomes, and an optional intent you enter are saved only on this device. Scroll Break does not read or save screen text, screenshots, or content you type in other apps, and does not upload or share this data.
</string>
